WEBVTT

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:22.620
That was a teleportation Code.

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:38.630
<i>Misa!</i>

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:41.240
With her body like that...

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:44.120
Misa...

00:00:56.510 --> 00:00:58.240
It's really coming down outside.

00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:05.510
For god's sake, where'd she go?

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:02.040
It wasn't Morishita or
Ichinose, but me...

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:04.760
It wasn't Morishita or
Ichinose, but me...

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:07.800
It wasn't Morishita or
Ichinose, but me...

00:03:08.860 --> 00:03:11.840
Yeah, it's hot. This is a problem.

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:14.530
Basically, since you have

00:03:14.530 --> 00:03:17.700
"seen" used with "was,"

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:20.270
you know "to be" is used
with the past participle.

00:03:20.270 --> 00:03:23.490
Thus, you have a sentence
in passive voice.

00:03:23.490 --> 00:03:26.970
So it makes sense to fill
in this space with

00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:31.690
"to" and the dictionary form of the
verb, which is the infinitive.

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:30.170
I guess Kaho-chan isn't coming...

00:03:31.780 --> 00:03:35.490
And I've tried calling both Misa-san and
Yumiko-chan, but I can't get through.

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:38.440
Maybe something happened.

00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:41.450
I'll try stopping by Misa-san's
place later.

00:03:56.910 --> 00:03:57.930
For the love of god...

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:05.630
Early this morning, security
guards discovered

00:04:05.630 --> 00:04:07.390
a large portion of the

00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:10.930
MTC building's roof hollowed-out
by an unknown party.

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:13.050
Authorities were contacted.

00:04:13.050 --> 00:04:16.290
However, no one in the building
or from the surrounding area

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:19.180
witnessed anything that would
carve such a hole.

00:04:19.180 --> 00:04:23.600
Police are investigating the matter
as a possible accident or crime.

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:29.080
I saw something shining
atop the building,

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:32.610
but no one else seemed to see it.

00:04:33.260 --> 00:04:35.420
I wonder what that was.

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:41.630
A light shining on the roof...

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:55.220
We finally cleaned it up.

00:04:56.010 --> 00:04:58.730
And now, thanks to that
burglar, it's a mess.

00:04:59.260 --> 00:05:00.220
God...

00:05:14.270 --> 00:05:16.590
We still had these?

00:05:20.690 --> 00:05:22.870
We don't need sixty of these!

00:05:22.870 --> 00:05:27.650
What kind of household would
buy curry in bulk?

00:05:27.650 --> 00:05:29.310
They were cheap.

00:05:29.310 --> 00:05:30.790
The taste won't change, either.

00:05:30.790 --> 00:05:33.900
And I thought we could have
everyone eat them.

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:36.600
That doesn't mean you can...
There are just too many.

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:40.580
But quantity doesn't
affect quality.

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:46.870
Curry is better when you
mix the spices yourself.

00:05:46.870 --> 00:05:49.010
If you really want to
cook that badly,

00:05:49.010 --> 00:05:51.820
I'll make the curry powder
for you myself.

00:05:52.500 --> 00:05:53.860
Thanks.

00:05:55.210 --> 00:05:56.770
I look forward to it.

00:05:58.600 --> 00:06:02.280
But my sister makes better curry.

00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:04.870
She doesn't look it, but
she cooks pretty well.

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:15.660
What's that?

00:06:15.660 --> 00:06:17.110
Bouillabaisse.

00:06:17.110 --> 00:06:18.990
What's up with the color?

00:06:18.990 --> 00:06:20.470
The soup's all green.

00:06:20.470 --> 00:06:23.270
I tried adding juice from green
vegetables. Healthy, right?

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:26.180
You're kidding?

00:06:26.180 --> 00:06:28.270
Try it.

00:06:37.750 --> 00:06:39.800
See? Told ya it was good.

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:47.120
Guess I've been force-fed some
weird stuff for a while...

00:06:47.780 --> 00:06:49.550
She just now got back?

00:06:58.820 --> 00:06:59.820
Yeah, I'm coming.

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:03.170
You lost your keys on top of that?

00:07:03.170 --> 00:07:04.760
You could have at least called-

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:14.700
You...

00:07:15.060 --> 00:07:17.730
Is Misa there?

00:07:17.730 --> 00:07:19.940
Sh-She's out...

00:07:19.940 --> 00:07:23.810
Did she come home
all of a sudden?

00:07:23.810 --> 00:07:28.020
No, she didn't. She's been
out since last night.

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:32.880
When I say "all of a sudden,"
I mean "all of a sudden"!

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:35.280
She hasn't come back all
of a sudden at all?!

00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:36.390
Huh?

00:07:36.950 --> 00:07:38.260
She hasn't!

00:07:45.650 --> 00:07:50.230
Mind if I come in and look
for her for awhile?

00:07:51.980 --> 00:07:53.230
Go ahead.

00:07:53.670 --> 00:07:55.220
Thanks.

00:08:56.140 --> 00:09:01.920
Do you have any idea where Misa
might go if she were in trouble?

00:09:02.280 --> 00:09:03.590
Normally, she'd go home, right?

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:06.160
I mean somewhere
other than that!

00:09:08.020 --> 00:09:10.420
Like in case of an emergency

00:09:10.420 --> 00:09:13.450
or if she were involved with some
sort of magical activation Code...

00:09:13.450 --> 00:09:15.450
Basically, if she were in trouble!

00:09:16.340 --> 00:09:18.900
Don't talk about magic
around me.

00:09:18.900 --> 00:09:20.980
Just give a serious answer!

00:09:23.850 --> 00:09:26.210
Home or the university...

00:09:26.210 --> 00:09:30.340
Maybe a computer company,
if they needed it.

00:09:30.840 --> 00:09:33.510
If that were the case, she would
have contacted you.

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:35.770
Then what? Another
crime or something?

00:09:35.770 --> 00:09:37.180
I've had enough of this!

00:09:37.540 --> 00:09:41.700
Please! Just think as hard
as you can, okay?

00:09:41.700 --> 00:09:44.010
This is a real emergency!

00:09:46.740 --> 00:09:49.750
I've done as much as I can,

00:09:49.750 --> 00:09:53.780
but I can't find her with
my senses alone.

00:10:02.440 --> 00:10:03.440
Akihabara.

00:10:04.290 --> 00:10:06.430
When emergencies arose
with her work,

00:10:06.430 --> 00:10:08.270
she often went there
to buy parts.

00:10:08.270 --> 00:10:09.940
That's it!

00:10:13.760 --> 00:10:16.560
I'm going to try to find Misa now,

00:10:16.560 --> 00:10:21.300
but I have something I
need to tell you first.

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:22.800
What is it?

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:35.820
I killed Misa.

00:10:46.950 --> 00:10:48.070
Huh?

00:11:02.990 --> 00:11:04.580
It's simple!

00:11:04.910 --> 00:11:09.090
All you have to do is arrange the Codes,
which I constructed, in the CPU.

00:11:09.430 --> 00:11:12.620
If you do that, you'll be
able to use magic, too.

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:17.570
Since you already know a bit, I'll
teach you quite a few, 'kay?

00:11:18.180 --> 00:11:20.850
The Code to connect
to the amulet...

00:11:24.430 --> 00:11:26.980
What good does it
do you to obtain

00:11:26.980 --> 00:11:32.150
the Sorceress's Library and update the
system that governs this world?

00:11:32.150 --> 00:11:34.700
There isn't any personal benefit.

00:11:35.020 --> 00:11:36.360
If you'll permit me to
engage in platitudes,

00:11:36.360 --> 00:11:39.640
I guess I would say it is to further
knowledge for all of mankind.

00:11:39.640 --> 00:11:41.920
So it's not for yourself?

00:11:42.320 --> 00:11:44.100
No, it is for me.

00:11:44.520 --> 00:11:50.230
Those who were born gifted, like yourself
and Anehara-san, might not understand.

00:11:50.230 --> 00:11:56.520
But I was born in China and went out
of my way to come to Akihabara.

00:11:56.520 --> 00:11:58.550
If Digitalis is revived,

00:11:58.550 --> 00:12:01.600
destruction and mass murder
will ensue in this town.

00:12:01.990 --> 00:12:05.550
There has never been a time when
wars were not fought.

00:12:05.550 --> 00:12:08.270
People are still born and people still die.

00:12:08.730 --> 00:12:12.250
There's no point in dwelling only
on the peace we see before us.

00:12:12.910 --> 00:12:13.990
I see.

00:12:14.830 --> 00:12:16.940
Digitalis Flammalacia.

00:12:17.620 --> 00:12:20.730
The reason she revived countless
times is because

00:12:20.730 --> 00:12:24.310
she stored the "Digitalis" program
outside of her body.

00:12:24.310 --> 00:12:28.370
So each time she died, she'd install it into a different one.

00:12:28.790 --> 00:12:33.400
The Sorceress's Library, which is just a
collection of information, is eternal.

00:12:33.820 --> 00:12:37.850
I guess it's about time we lured out the casing.

00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:59.420
I've been here before...

00:12:59.820 --> 00:13:02.270
We ate hamburgers together,

00:13:04.850 --> 00:13:06.870
and she was there
to hold my hand.

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:12.250
But right now...

00:13:18.270 --> 00:13:21.090
You followed me?

00:13:24.890 --> 00:13:28.070
So, you're going to stay
with me again?

00:13:30.500 --> 00:13:31.550
Thanks.

00:13:37.400 --> 00:13:40.360
Two Codes. No doubt about it.

00:13:43.470 --> 00:13:46.310
We're going to Akihabara.

00:13:56.050 --> 00:13:59.640
I killed Misa.

00:14:01.530 --> 00:14:02.980
She's completely nuts.

00:14:02.980 --> 00:14:04.640
Hello!

00:14:05.550 --> 00:14:08.330
Lots of guests today.

00:14:19.730 --> 00:14:22.870
Misa's not here today?

00:14:24.950 --> 00:14:26.930
Looks like she's dead.

00:14:31.830 --> 00:14:34.930
That's what that silver-haired
girl said, anyway.

00:14:35.210 --> 00:14:37.540
Yumiko-chan said...

00:14:40.960 --> 00:14:42.940
That can't be true, right?

00:14:43.540 --> 00:14:46.950
It's true she hasn't been here
since yesterday, though.

00:14:48.250 --> 00:14:49.600
I...

00:14:49.600 --> 00:14:51.210
killed-

00:14:51.370 --> 00:14:52.500
She ki-

00:14:54.030 --> 00:14:56.170
She said she died,

00:14:56.650 --> 00:14:59.400
but it looked like she
was looking for her.

00:15:00.510 --> 00:15:02.700
I really don't get it.

00:15:05.040 --> 00:15:08.220
Oh, yeah! You want
some curry powder?

00:15:08.530 --> 00:15:10.480
Huh? Curry?

00:15:10.480 --> 00:15:11.400
Huh?

00:15:11.680 --> 00:15:14.180
I've got a ton and don't know
what to do with it.

00:15:14.650 --> 00:15:17.350
Just one would have
been enough, but...

00:15:22.160 --> 00:15:25.210
Wow, I wonder how many curry nuts

00:15:25.210 --> 00:15:28.590
it took to make this much curry powder.

00:15:32.350 --> 00:15:36.490
Well, they make curry powder
by crushing up curry nuts.

00:15:36.780 --> 00:15:39.470
There's a bunch of curry
trees in India,

00:15:39.470 --> 00:15:42.510
and the monks pray every
year for a good harvest.

00:15:44.360 --> 00:15:45.990
Are you stupid?

00:15:46.850 --> 00:15:50.330
Curry is just a bunch of different
spices mixed together.

00:15:50.330 --> 00:15:52.380
There's no such thing
as a curry tree.

00:15:52.720 --> 00:15:54.470
No way!

00:15:54.470 --> 00:15:56.910
You haven't actually
seen one, have you?

00:15:56.910 --> 00:15:59.370
Kaho-chan lied to me.

00:15:59.370 --> 00:16:01.650
Even an elementary-school
kid wouldn't believe that.

00:16:01.650 --> 00:16:03.140
But...

00:16:03.500 --> 00:16:06.880
Kaho-chan...

00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:10.650
Wh-What?

00:16:13.290 --> 00:16:16.040
You don't have to laugh so much!

00:16:16.430 --> 00:16:18.140
No, I'm sorry.

00:16:24.900 --> 00:16:26.170
Let's go.

00:16:26.550 --> 00:16:28.890
Huh? Where?

00:16:29.430 --> 00:16:31.420
To look for my sister.

00:16:33.780 --> 00:16:35.010
Okay!

00:16:37.100 --> 00:16:39.930
Log in to the school... You have
to secure addresses...

00:16:39.930 --> 00:16:43.420
Send a request... The addresses
will respond...

00:16:43.420 --> 00:16:46.680
Properly secured addresses
won't respond...

00:16:46.680 --> 00:16:50.440
Use a brute-force attack... Then use
that as a proxy to go overseas...

00:16:53.770 --> 00:16:55.420
All that's left...

00:17:00.840 --> 00:17:02.580
My foot cramped up.

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:13.260
The line of a weak Code... I have to
make sure not to lose sight of it.

00:17:19.240 --> 00:17:20.590
Morishita Koyomi

00:17:21.750 --> 00:17:22.700
Hi?

00:17:23.590 --> 00:17:26.100
Ah, Yumiko-chan? You
finally picked up.

00:17:26.100 --> 00:17:27.700
Do you need something?

00:17:29.040 --> 00:17:31.890
Um, I'm headed to Akihabara
right now...

00:17:31.890 --> 00:17:34.490
Oh, Soshiro is with
me, too, um...

00:17:34.490 --> 00:17:36.640
I'm going to hang up if you
don't need anything.

00:17:36.640 --> 00:17:38.110
I'm busy.

00:17:38.110 --> 00:17:40.410
Y-You're looking for
Misa-san, right?

00:17:41.570 --> 00:17:43.080
I thought it would

00:17:43.080 --> 00:17:45.610
be better for all of us to look, instead
of just you out there alone.

00:17:45.610 --> 00:17:47.840
It'd be less lonely that way.

00:17:47.840 --> 00:17:49.860
So, um...

00:17:49.860 --> 00:17:51.410
I got it.

00:17:52.220 --> 00:17:56.400
Let's meet in front of the
donut shop at 6:30.

00:17:56.400 --> 00:17:59.140
If either of us figures something out
before then, we'll call each other.

00:17:59.140 --> 00:18:00.210
Got it?

00:18:00.210 --> 00:18:01.330
Y-Yeah.

00:18:01.330 --> 00:18:02.270
Later, then.

00:18:05.510 --> 00:18:07.820
Out of all the times...

00:18:09.570 --> 00:18:11.600
She hung up.

00:18:11.600 --> 00:18:14.720
That's why I told you to
just leave her alone.

00:18:14.720 --> 00:18:15.760
But...

00:18:17.710 --> 00:18:19.770
That was dangerous!

00:18:19.770 --> 00:18:20.870
Hurry and pick up already.

00:18:22.620 --> 00:18:24.290
Hallo...

00:18:24.290 --> 00:18:25.430
There you are.

00:18:25.430 --> 00:18:28.210
Oh, Kaho-chan! Why didn't you
show up at school today?

00:18:28.210 --> 00:18:29.710
Are you sick?

00:18:30.200 --> 00:18:33.110
I'll explain the details
later. Where are you?

00:18:33.110 --> 00:18:35.310
A-Akihabara.

00:18:36.470 --> 00:18:39.320
Then let's meet up close
to Shichibu Electronics.

00:18:39.320 --> 00:18:41.360
Huh? Where's Shichibu Electronics-

00:18:51.560 --> 00:18:54.080
There it is. We're finally here.

00:18:54.080 --> 00:18:56.360
I told you it was in the complete
opposite direction!

00:18:56.360 --> 00:18:57.570
But...

00:18:57.880 --> 00:18:59.990
Oh, Kaho-chan, found you!

00:18:59.990 --> 00:19:01.210
Morishita, you're slow.

00:19:01.560 --> 00:19:04.240
No one would normally know
where this place is.

00:19:04.240 --> 00:19:04.870
Really?

00:19:04.870 --> 00:19:08.580
God, we wasted so much time.
Let's hurry up and look for her!

00:19:08.580 --> 00:19:10.300
Hey, let's rest a bit...

00:19:10.300 --> 00:19:11.250
Look for her?

00:19:11.650 --> 00:19:16.240
Yeah. It's really bad, Kaho-chan.
Misa-san disappeared!

00:19:16.240 --> 00:19:17.810
Disappeared?

00:19:17.810 --> 00:19:20.170
Yumiko-chan's like, she's dead...

00:19:20.170 --> 00:19:21.170
Ichinose is?

00:19:21.170 --> 00:19:23.040
No, Misa-san was the
one who died.

00:19:23.040 --> 00:19:24.990
But, she's not actually dead.

00:19:24.990 --> 00:19:28.120
Soshiro-san's probably looking
for Yumiko-chan, I think.

00:19:28.120 --> 00:19:29.820
We're looking for Ichinose?

00:19:29.820 --> 00:19:33.640
Uh, I mean... I mean...
Let's find her together!

00:19:33.640 --> 00:19:34.240
Hey!

00:19:34.240 --> 00:19:34.950
I got it.

00:19:34.950 --> 00:19:35.760
You did?

00:19:35.760 --> 00:19:38.210
Ichinose told you, Soshiro,
that Misa-san died,

00:19:38.210 --> 00:19:40.260
but seems to be looking
for where she went,

00:19:40.260 --> 00:19:43.270
so Koyomi said we should all look
for her together, I believe.

00:19:43.810 --> 00:19:45.350
You're pretty amazing...

00:19:45.920 --> 00:19:48.310
So, we meet again, girl.

00:19:57.800 --> 00:19:59.500
You know each other?

00:19:59.500 --> 00:20:05.550
When I revived the Sorceress's Library,
I mistook her for Anehara Misa.

00:20:06.420 --> 00:20:07.560
Why are you...

00:20:07.950 --> 00:20:12.560
He brought me back to
life with this sword.

00:20:13.920 --> 00:20:15.170
What's up with him?

00:20:15.170 --> 00:20:16.880
I can't see him.

00:20:16.880 --> 00:20:17.570
Can't see what?

00:20:20.590 --> 00:20:23.110
You're the burglar who
broke into our house!

00:20:23.630 --> 00:20:25.840
So, you're the younger brother?

00:20:26.230 --> 00:20:27.800
Younger brother?

00:20:27.800 --> 00:20:31.090
I'm sorry, but I won't be
giving back the sword.

00:20:31.340 --> 00:20:34.300
You're the one... You're the
one who took my sister!

00:20:34.300 --> 00:20:35.300
Yes?

00:20:35.580 --> 00:20:37.960
What did you do with her?

00:20:37.960 --> 00:20:39.080
No, stop!

00:20:49.790 --> 00:20:50.450
Hey!

00:20:50.450 --> 00:20:51.100
What's going on?

00:20:51.100 --> 00:20:52.220
What's that?

00:20:56.380 --> 00:20:57.500
Hey, let go of me!

00:20:58.490 --> 00:21:01.680
Put this around your neck,
as soon as possible.

00:21:02.440 --> 00:21:04.430
Now's not the time!

00:21:04.760 --> 00:21:07.030
Morishita can't. You do it.

00:21:10.040 --> 00:21:11.540
Wait.

00:21:11.900 --> 00:21:13.990
We should withdraw for now, Huang.

00:21:16.140 --> 00:21:19.200
There was a strange
Code just now.

00:21:19.200 --> 00:21:20.480
But...

00:21:20.480 --> 00:21:23.770
I have more knowledge
of magic than you do.

00:21:24.650 --> 00:21:26.010
Very well.

00:21:28.790 --> 00:21:30.030
Hey, wait!

00:21:30.030 --> 00:21:31.230
Hurry up!

00:21:32.970 --> 00:21:34.360
Out of the way!

00:21:36.080 --> 00:21:38.510
There. You're happy now, right?

00:21:43.730 --> 00:21:44.690
Damn it.

00:21:45.260 --> 00:21:46.750
Thank goodness...

00:21:46.750 --> 00:21:49.480
I believe that was the
best choice just now.

00:21:49.480 --> 00:21:50.940
What are you saying?

00:21:50.940 --> 00:21:53.450
We might have finally
found a clue...

00:21:53.450 --> 00:21:55.010
What gives?

00:21:54.270 --> 00:21:56.980
Well, you know how it goes.

00:21:58.940 --> 00:22:01.000
Over here!

00:22:06.870 --> 00:22:09.000
Huh, Misa-san?

00:22:11.360 --> 00:22:13.640
How ya been?

00:23:46.290 --> 00:23:49.860
The hacker who plans on bringing the
legendary sorceress back to life...

00:23:49.860 --> 00:23:52.900
Doing so means the destruction
of the world.

00:23:52.900 --> 00:23:55.800
The Modern-Day mage who
returned to stop him

00:23:55.800 --> 00:23:58.750
will fight alongside a Classical
Magic mage.

00:24:04.570 --> 00:24:07.080
Subtitles

00:24:07.980 --> 00:24:12.010
Hello! This is the season
for dumplings!

00:24:12.010 --> 00:24:13.910
Morishita Koyomi here!

00:24:13.910 --> 00:24:16.750
Hi! Anehara Misa here.

00:24:16.750 --> 00:24:21.760
Koyomi, do you know what
each of the subtitles are?

00:24:21.760 --> 00:24:25.550
It seems like English...

00:24:25.550 --> 00:24:30.660
Well, yeah. You can tell by looking.
I'm asking what the words means.

00:24:30.660 --> 00:24:35.350
I have no clue!

00:24:36.360 --> 00:24:38.180
I thought so!

00:24:38.180 --> 00:24:41.180
Sorry for not knowing anything...

00:24:41.530 --> 00:24:44.860
Some of the subtitles for <i>Yoku
Wakaru Gendai Mahou</i>

00:24:44.860 --> 00:24:50.060
use computer terminology
or slang.

00:24:50.060 --> 00:24:52.540
Really?

00:24:52.540 --> 00:24:56.410
For example, in ep. 1,
the title "hello, world"

00:24:56.410 --> 00:24:59.430
is the standard string used when
you're programming in

00:24:59.430 --> 00:25:05.130
a language for the first time and
want to make sure it works.

00:25:05.130 --> 00:25:09.720
For the most part, you often see
it in C and older languages.

00:25:09.720 --> 00:25:14.530
Teacher, what's C?

00:25:14.530 --> 00:25:15.370
Google it.

00:25:16.850 --> 00:25:20.900
Kaho-chan told me that, too!

00:25:20.900 --> 00:25:24.510
Also, the name of this episode,
"quick-and-dirty,"

00:25:24.510 --> 00:25:27.860
is the name of DOS. If you
take the letters QDOS,

00:25:27.860 --> 00:25:31.040
it forms "Quick-and-Dirty
Operating System."

00:25:31.040 --> 00:25:33.280
Or, QDOS.

00:25:33.280 --> 00:25:38.210
Basically, it just means
an improvised OS.

00:25:38.210 --> 00:25:41.130
I see!

00:25:41.130 --> 00:25:45.950
Sakurazaka-san, the author of the original
works, named each of the episodes!

00:25:46.310 --> 00:25:49.220
Okay! That's it for today!

00:25:49.220 --> 00:25:53.610
Please look up the other
subtitles, too.

00:25:53.610 --> 00:25:58.530
Um, Teacher, what does
google it mean?

00:25:58.530 --> 00:26:00.380
Google googling it.

00:26:00.380 --> 00:26:03.150
No!

00:26:03.150 --> 00:26:05.550
See you next week.

00:26:05.550 --> 00:26:08.540
Bye-bye!
